# TODO_progress_display
#
# Design: DAG progress visualization with "power flow" rendering.
#
# Replace verbose line-dump shell output with a live DAG visualization
# that shows nodes lighting up as execution progresses — think SimCity
# (2013) power grid flowing through infrastructure.
#
# Architecture:
#   1. Symbol system in core/ir (visual vocabulary for the whole codebase)
#   2. Renderer-agnostic progress data model
#   3. Carriage-return terminal renderer with dynamic ASCII art mode
#   4. Integration with existing rendering infrastructure
#      (Renderable trait, language module, CI rendering, dag-viz)

## Problem

Current shell output dumps sequential log lines:

    [parse_read_files]
      contents: {234 entries}
    [render_markdown]
      markdown: # Code Snapshot...
    [execute_gist]
      exit_code: 0
      stderr: - Creating gist snapshot.md
    [parse_gist_response]
      url: https://gist.github.com/...

This is functional but:
- No sense of overall progress or structure
- Can't see which nodes are waiting, running, or done
- No visual relationship between nodes (edges are invisible)
- Long pipelines produce walls of text that scroll off screen

## Four-layer architecture

    ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │  Layer 4: Renderers (terminal, web, CI)             │
    │  - Carriage-return terminal (emoji default)          │
    │  - Dynamic ASCII art mode (cellular automaton)       │
    │  - Web: JSON/SSE → browser SVG (reuse dag-viz)      │
    │  - CI: feeds into CiRenderer providers               │
    ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
    │  Layer 3: DagProgress (renderer-agnostic state)     │
    │  - NodeState, EdgeState, timing, output summaries   │
    │  - Snapshot-based: renderers poll or subscribe       │
    ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
    │  Layer 2: ProgressObserver (execution hook)         │
    │  - Plugs into execute_flat() loop                   │
    │  - Emits events: NodeStarted, NodeCompleted, etc.   │
    ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
    │  Layer 1: Symbol System (core/ir — visual vocab)    │
    │  - SymbolId, Symbol, SymbolSet, Tier, SemanticColor │
    │  - Shared by ALL display code across the codebase   │
    │  - Integrates with language module + Renderable      │
    └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

