### Why in core/ir?

The symbol module belongs in core/ir (not in a renderer crate) because:
- It's a vocabulary, not a rendering engine — any crate can use it
- The language module already models format-specific visual concerns
  (comment syntax, naming conventions) in core/ir as SubDags
- CI context, error messages, and future tools will all want consistent
  symbol references without depending on a renderer crate
- SymbolId + SymbolSet follow the same pattern as TypeId + TypeRegistry
- The Renderable trait is already in core/ir — symbols extend the
  rendering vocabulary in the same crate

