## Layer 4: Terminal Renderer (carriage-return based)

### Rendering modes

The terminal renderer supports multiple visual modes, selectable at
construction time. All modes use the same DagProgress data model and
SymbolSet vocabulary — they differ only in how they present it.

```rust
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy)]
pub enum RenderMode {
    /// Standard mode — symbol-per-state, clean layout.
    /// Uses SymbolSet tier directly (emoji/unicode/ascii).
    Standard,

    /// Dynamic ASCII art mode — cellular automaton effects.
    /// Edge flow uses propagating cell patterns.
    /// Node transitions use Game-of-Life-style animations.
    Dynamic,

    /// Compact mode — single-line summary.
    /// Good for small terminal windows or embedding.
    Compact,
}
```

### Standard mode: carriage return + ANSI

The renderer uses `\r` (carriage return) to overwrite terminal lines
in place. For multi-line display, it uses ANSI cursor-up (`\x1b[A`)
to move back to the top of the display area and rewrite. This gives
a live-updating display without any TUI framework dependency.

The symbol system's Emoji tier is the default — modern emojis make
the display visually striking. We control the environment so
compatibility is not a constraint.

