## CI renderer integration

The CI providers (GitHub Actions, GitLab CI) already have rendering
code in core/ir/src/transport/ci/. The progress system integrates
with them through the existing CiContext:

### Current CI rendering

CiContext already emits:
- Collapsible groups around nodes (::group:: / section_start)
- Error/warning annotations with file locations
- Nested group hierarchy

### Progress system integration

The ProgressObserver can feed into CiContext directly:

```rust
pub struct CiProgressObserver {
    ci: CiContext,
    symbols: &'static SymbolSet,
    tier: Tier,  // ASCII tier for CI logs
}

impl ProgressObserver for CiProgressObserver {
    fn on_node_start(&mut self, node_id: &NodeId) {
        // Emit CI group with symbol prefix
        let sym = self.symbols.render_at(SymbolId::NodeRunning, self.tier);
        self.ci.start_group(&format!("{} {}", sym, node_id));
    }

    fn on_node_complete(&mut self, node_id: &NodeId, summary: OutputSummary) {
        let sym = self.symbols.render_at(SymbolId::NodeCompleted, self.tier);
        self.ci.end_group();
        // Emit summary as CI annotation
        for field in &summary.fields {
            self.ci.notice(&format!("{} {}: {}", sym, field.name, field.preview));
        }
    }

    fn on_node_failed(&mut self, node_id: &NodeId, error: &str) {
        let sym = self.symbols.render_at(SymbolId::NodeFailed, self.tier);
        self.ci.end_group();
        self.ci.error(&format!("{} {} failed: {}", sym, node_id, error));
    }
}
```

This means CI output gets the same semantic symbols as terminal output
(at the ASCII tier), and the existing CiContext infrastructure handles
the provider-specific formatting.

