## Web renderer (future — extends dag-viz)

The existing dag-viz tool (gunbc-dag/src/bin/dag-viz.rs) already
generates interactive HTML with Mermaid flowcharts. The web renderer
extends this with live execution state:

### Current dag-viz capabilities

- Renders all workspace DAGs as Mermaid flowcharts
- Dark-themed HTML with CSS variables
- Zoom/pan controls (mouse wheel + drag)
- Multiple diagram sections with navigation

### Progress system extension

    1. DagProgress serializes to JSON (already has Serialize)
    2. SSE/WebSocket streams progress events to browser
    3. JavaScript consumes events and updates Mermaid node styles
    4. SemanticColor maps to CSS classes (already defined in dag-viz's
       CSS variable system: --bg, --text, --accent, --highlight)
    5. Mermaid style classes for node states:
       classDef pending fill:#666,color:#999
       classDef running fill:#f39c12,color:#fff
       classDef completed fill:#2ecc71,color:#fff
       classDef failed fill:#e74c3c,color:#fff

    6. Edge flow animation via Mermaid's linkStyle:
       linkStyle 0 stroke:#f39c12,stroke-width:3px  (flowing)
       linkStyle 0 stroke:#2ecc71,stroke-width:2px  (done)

The symbol system's emoji tier maps directly to HTML text content,
so the same symbols appear in both terminal and web.

